/*
  DriveScore.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0082 · DriveScore (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The web source
  (components/data-display/DriveScore.tsx) carries six pieces of visible copy, mirrored here with the
  SAME keys the web `t()` calls use:

    • driveScore.title              — the breakdown heading ("Drive Score").
    • driveScore.score              — the caption under the gauge number ("Score").
    • driveScore.efficiency         — the 40-point axis label ("Efficiency").
    • driveScore.speedDiscipline    — a 20-point axis label ("Speed Discipline").
    • driveScore.rangePreservation  — a 20-point axis label ("Range Preservation").
    • driveScore.tripLength         — a 20-point axis label ("Trip Length").

  The web renders the numeric score / "value/max" readouts from JS-formatted numbers (not translated
  copy), so they carry no key. Two extra VoiceOver-only formats make the gauge and the breakdown rows
  first-class accessibility elements (the web relies on the visible text being read aloud):

    • driveScore.a11y.score      — "Drive Score: {total} out of {max}" (positional %1$d / %2$d).
    • driveScore.a11y.breakdown  — "{axis}: {value} of {max} points" (positional %1$@ / %2$d / %3$d).

  These entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are
  kept in a per-surface table ("DriveScore") so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings.
*/

